msgid ""
"Quarkus Insights #247: Agentic Orchestration with LangChain4j and Kubernetes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This summary was generated using AI, reviewed by humans - https://youtube."
"com/live/oX2GP7D28DE[watch the video] for the full story."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In episode 247 of Quarkus Insights, https://www.linkedin.com/in/javajon/"
"[Jonathan Johnson], an independent software architect and adjunct professor "
"at https://www.trincoll.edu/[Trinity College] (Connecticut), shared his "
"innovative work on distributed agentic AI systems running on https://"
"kubernetes.io/[Kubernetes] with https://quarkus.io/[Quarkus] and https://"
"docs.langchain4j.dev/[LangChain4j]."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Journey: From Spring Boot to Quarkus"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Jonathan's journey began with a home lab project using Spring Boot and "
"Spring AI. After attending a Connecticut Java Users Group talk by Eric "
"Deandrea (from the Quarkus team), he was inspired to explore LangChain4j "
"with Quarkus. Using https://claude.ai/[Claude AI] for code conversion, he "
"successfully migrated his Spring Boot application to Quarkus with "
"LangChain4j in approximately one hour."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Key migration benefits observed:\n"
"- Faster startup times\n"
"- Reduced memory footprint\n"
"- Lower CPU usage\n"
"- Native compilation with https://www.graalvm.org/[GraalVM] support"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Home Lab Setup"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Jonathan built an impressive home lab infrastructure to support his "
"distributed AI experiments:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Three custom-built rigs** running https://www.proxmox.com/[Proxmox] as the "
"hypervisor"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**GPU resources**: https://www.nvidia.com/[NVIDIA] 4090 (24GB) and 5090 "
"(32GB) for local model inference"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Total memory**: 480GB RAM across the cluster"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Storage**: 70TB NAS using https://www.truenas.com/[TrueNAS]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Kubernetes**: Vanilla Kubernetes deployed via https://kubernetes.io/docs/"
"setup/production-environment/tools/kubeadm/[kubeadm]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Infrastructure as Code**: https://opentofu.org/[OpenTofu] scripts for "
"reproducible deployments"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The entire setup runs https://ollama.com/[Ollama] on Kubernetes with GPU "
"passthrough, enabling local LLM inference without cloud dependencies."
msgstr ""

msgid "Distributed Agentic Architecture: A Different Approach"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Rather than using traditional LangChain4j annotations for sequential or "
"parallel agent pipelines within a single application, Jonathan implemented a "
"**distributed round-table architecture** using https://nats.io/[NATS] "
"messaging:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Traditional Approach (Monolithic)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Distributed Approach (Kubemoot)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Agents as Kubernetes pods**: Each agent runs as an independent container"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**NATS messaging**: Agents communicate via distributed messaging (not inter-"
"process)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Democratic coordination**: Agents self-select to contribute based on their "
"expertise"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Round-table pattern**: Similar to Reddit threads where experts chime in"
msgstr ""

msgid "Architecture Components"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Coordinator Agent**: Interprets incoming questions and broadcasts to the "
"agent pool"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Specialist Agents**: Each has domain expertise (Kubernetes, Proxmox, SQL, "
"etc.)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**MCP Tools**: Agents have access to https://modelcontextprotocol.io/[Model "
"Context Protocol] tools"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Prompts as ConfigMaps**: Stored as Kubernetes YAML manifests, not compiled "
"code"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Kubemoot Operator**: Custom Kubernetes operator managing the agentic "
"system"
msgstr ""

msgid "Key Technical Insights"
msgstr ""

msgid "Prompt Engineering with ADL"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Jonathan adopted the **Architecture Definition Language (ADL)** from https://"
"www.developertoarchitect.com/[Mark Richards and Neal Ford] for more "
"structured prompting:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Moved from informal English prose to semi-formal ADL specifications"
msgstr ""

msgid "Observed significant improvements in response quality and speed"
msgstr ""

msgid "Better agent comprehension compared to unstructured prompts"
msgstr ""

msgid "Performance Considerations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Challenges with distributed agents:**\n"
"- Initial democratic approach was slow (15+ minutes for simple queries)\n"
"- Each agent loading context independently created overhead\n"
"- Trade-off between flexibility and performance"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Optimizations:**\n"
"- Selective agent participation based on question relevance\n"
"- Agents can \"bow out\" if not relevant to the query\n"
"- Running entirely on local GPUs (no cloud API costs)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Development Workflow"
msgstr ""

msgid "Jonathan emphasized modern development practices:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Vibe coding with Claude**: Rapid prototyping and code generation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Kanban boards in https://obsidian.md/[Obsidian]**: Task tracking for AI-"
"assisted development"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**GitOps**: All infrastructure changes via OpenTofu and https://git-scm.com/"
"[Git] commits"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**CI/CD**: https://github.com/features/actions[GitHub Actions] + https://"
"fluxcd.io/[Flux] for automated deployments"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**No imperative kubectl commands**: Everything through infrastructure as "
"code"
msgstr ""

msgid "Lessons Learned"
msgstr ""

msgid "AI-Assisted Development"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Voice-to-text tools (like https://github.com/kitlangton/Hex[Hex]) reduce "
"typing fatigue during long AI sessions"
msgstr ""

msgid "Maintain discipline: avoid letting AI make imperative cluster changes"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use Kanban boards to track AI-generated tasks and prevent context loss"
msgstr ""

msgid "Set clear boundaries in prompts (e.g., \"always use GitOps\")"
msgstr ""

